From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Unwind the probe error paths

sunxi_mmc_resource_request() leaves the module and bus clocks on and
the reset released. If the interrupt request, the descriptor
allocation, mmc_of_parse(), sunxi_mmc_init_host() or mmc_add_host()
fails afterwards, probe returns with the controller still running. A
failed mmc_add_host() also leaves runtime PM enabled, and the next bind
warns about an unbalanced pm_runtime_enable().

Release in reverse order of acquisition, with a label per step as
mtk-sd does: runtime PM only once it was enabled, then the descriptor
memory, then the interrupt and the clocks, as sunxi_mmc_remove() does.
The interrupt request in sunxi_mmc_resource_request() jumps to the
label that switches the clocks off.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with a test-only change
that fails each probe step on demand; after every failed bind of the SD
and the eMMC controller the clocks are off and the reset is asserted,
and the next bind works without an unbalanced pm_runtime_enable()
warning.

Fixes: 3cbcb16095f9 ("mmc: sunxi: Add driver for SD/MMC hosts found on Allwinner sunxi SoCs")
Fixes: 9a8e1e8cc2c0 ("mmc: sunxi: Add runtime_pm support")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
index fe4c0f6d73f3..c30eacb660f7 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -1354,8 +1354,12 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_resource_request(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host,
 		goto error_disable_mmc;
 	}
 
-	return devm_request_threaded_irq(&pdev->dev, host->irq, sunxi_mmc_irq,
+	ret = devm_request_threaded_irq(&pdev->dev, host->irq, sunxi_mmc_irq,
 			sunxi_mmc_handle_manual_stop, 0, "sunxi-mmc", host);
+	if (ret)
+		goto error_disable_mmc;
+
+	return 0;
 
 error_disable_mmc:
 	sunxi_mmc_disable(host);
@@ -1385,9 +1389,11 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	host->sg_cpu = dma_alloc_coherent(&pdev->dev, PAGE_SIZE,
 					  &host->sg_dma, GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!host->sg_cpu)
-		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -ENOMEM,
-				     "Failed to allocate DMA descriptor mem\n");
+	if (!host->sg_cpu) {
+		ret = dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -ENOMEM,
+				    "Failed to allocate DMA descriptor mem\n");
+		goto error_disable_mmc;
+	}
 
 	if (host->cfg->ccu_has_timings_switch) {
 		/*
@@ -1467,7 +1473,7 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ret = mmc_add_host(mmc);
 	if (ret)
-		goto error_free_dma;
+		goto error_disable_pm;
 
 	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "initialized, max. request size: %u KB%s\n",
 		 mmc->max_req_size >> 10,
@@ -1475,8 +1481,13 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	return 0;
 
+error_disable_pm:
+	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
 error_free_dma:
 	dma_free_coherent(&pdev->dev, PAGE_SIZE, host->sg_cpu, host->sg_dma);
+error_disable_mmc:
+	disable_irq(host->irq);
+	sunxi_mmc_disable(host);
 	return ret;
 }
 
